+// COGBox SDK patch 106 (GitHub #329): a Gears 3 save set signed with a key COGBox can't name (an earlier online account
+// after a new one was made, a save from another PC or console, an old backup put back) used to be left alone, and Gears 3
+// then reset it and wrote fresh files over it - the progress was gone.
+//
+// CogAdoptSaveFiles re-signs one set for to_key without knowing its old key (the data is never changed, only the
+// 20-byte signature), but only a whole, plausible save: PlayerStorage.dat alone (4 KB - 64 KB), or the full profile set
+// 63E83FFF + 63E83FFE + 63E83FFD (each at most 1000 bytes); nothing all zero; every file readable (Refused /
+// ReadFailed otherwise, nothing written). files[0] is first copied to <file>.cogbox-adopted-<stamp> (a new name each
+// time, never replacing anything), then written through <file>.cogbox-tmp and renamed over the original. AlreadyDone
+// when the set is signed for to_key already.
+ResignResult CogAdoptSaveFiles(const std::vector<std::filesystem::path>& files, uint64_t to_key);
+// Every Gears 3 save set under user_data_root not signed for run_key is adopted as above, once: the body of each adopted
+// set is noted in <user_data_root>/cogbox-save-adopted, and a noted body found signed with another key again is left
+// alone (the game signs with a key COGBox doesn't predict - no loop). Never throws.
+void CogAdoptGears3Saves(const std::filesystem::path& user_data_root, uint64_t profile_xuid, uint64_t run_key);
